	(footprint "cec-Connector_Blade:TE_63951-1_FASTON_Tab_250x032_RA_THT"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "80a88c43-df7c-4333-ae55-8d45db89c6a0")
		(at 5.15 17.04)
		(descr "TE Connectivity 63951-1 FASTON .250 RIGHT-ANGLE PC board tab -- TE dwg C=63951 rev L2, App Spec 114-2115. The part is a FLAT IN-PLANE L stamping (0.83/0.77mm thick throughout, no out-of-plane bend): two barbed legs (5.08mm+/-0.08 pitch, 1.40mm+/-0.05 PCB holes, 3.81mm below the seating face) hang off one end of the strip, and the 6.35mm+/-0.08 blade runs ALONG the strip/leg-pitch axis past the blade-side leg to the tip. Blade width band sits 2.54..8.89mm off the seating face (8.89 = TE 'Profile Height from PCB'; 2.54 = 8.89 - 6.35), so the blade STANDS OFF the mounting face -- it never lies against it. MOUNTING ORIENTATION ON THIS PLATFORM (owner sketch, 2026-07-05, docs/standard-tier-review/blade-fit-check-2026-07-04.md addendum 3): legs horizontal through a VERTICAL daughterboard face, leg pitch VERTICAL (stacked one above the other), blade pointing STRAIGHT DOWN past the board's bottom edge at the 2.54-8.89mm Z-standoff, dropping broadside into a main-board Keystone 3586 clip's top-entry jaws. Local frame: origin = leg-pair midpoint; +Y = the blade/descend direction (board-down); the stamping plane is PERPENDICULAR to the board, so the 2D artwork is the part's thin projection band. Dims read off the dwg: tip at +15.75 from origin (= 20.32 cut-off - 7.11 cut-end-to-blade-side-leg + 2.54; chain-dim reading cross-checked against the drawn leg position at ~22% of part length and the 1217061-1 sibling's identical pattern -- flagged for the OQ-86 sample check, a small error here shifts assembly FLOAT, not clip engagement); carrier-side stub to -4.57 (7.11 - 5.08 + 2.54); shoulder (full-height, face-contacting) region ends 3.33-3.48 past the blade-side leg (+5.87..+6.02, tick at +5.95); detent hole 1.78mm dia at 7.92 from the tip (+7.83, drawn on the blade width-centre per the dwg view -- the dwg's 7.11 [.280] vertical dim may place it 1.78 below the blade top edge instead; cosmetic-only here, Fab ghost art).")
